        en: "Lovers of nature and authenticity: the beaches and plains of northern Tunisia will win you over — wild bays, forests and vast fields of vines and wheat. On the sea's edge, Bizerte, guardian of the Mediterranean, is a historic city full of charm. And this green region shelters two UNESCO World Heritage sites: the archaeological one, the Roman city of Dougga, and the natural one, Lake Ichkeul and its surrounding park, which draws migratory birds in their thousands.",
