        en: "Walk in the oasis of Gabes with its hundreds of thousands of palms, in whose shade many fruit trees grow; in early summer enjoy the flowering pomegranates that in autumn bear fruit full of sweet juice. Explore the winding lanes and covered passages of the old Menzel quarter, and in the colourful souk of Jara buy spices and henna powder, the dye plant harvested in the oasis. Gabes has beautiful beaches where flamingos and herons abound. Inland, the old Berber villages clinging to the hills blend into the rocky landscape, and this region hides one of the most curious sites in Tunisia: Matmata, where the ground is pierced by craters dug into the soft rock — in fact the courtyards of the cave dwellings, where people live in underground rooms to escape the fierce heat.",
