        en: "Walk out to visit the various ksour and the mountain villages, then see the Memory of the Earth museum in Tataouine with its dinosaur fossils and meteorites found in the region. Watch the weaving of the flij, the long strips that assembled make a Bedouin tent, and visit the weekly market where farmers and herders meet. Do not miss the Ksour Festival: you will see a re-enactment of the harvest-storing celebrations and hear the traditional music and songs of the south-east (in March). If you love plants and wildlife, explore the Sidi Toui national park, and a trip westwards brings you to the oasis of Ksar Ghilane, on the boundary between the stony desert and the sand desert.",
